  "comment": "The Real-time Transport Protocol ( RTP ) defines a standardized packet format for delivering audio and video over the Internet . It was developed by the Audio-Video Transport Working Group of the IETF and first published in 1996 as RFC 1889, and superseded by RFC 3550 in 2003. RTP is used extensively in communication and entertainment systems that involve streaming media , such as telephony ,",
